{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_tPqBhGmtKOQxUbtBEc9CkgRH|fc_0b92182eacec1870016a957fd39c1487d282f54a08d2b43c35","toolName":"read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[doc_code_discrepancies.csv#03B8]\n1:claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n2:MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths,README.md:6,minisvc.config:load_settings parses readonly; minisvc.cli:main ignores Settings.readonly after load; minisvc.api.handlers:create_order always calls OrderRepository.save without a readonly check.,contradicted,Operators may believe writes are disabled when order creation still persists rows.\n3:create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response,README.md:7,minisvc.api.handlers:create_order calls repo.save(order) exactly once; minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save performs one sqlite3 insert and has no retry loop or exception handling.,contradicted,Transient database failures surface directly and the service may be less resilient than documented.\n4:Audit events are stored in a durable audit table,README.md:8,minisvc.audit:order_event only returns a dict; minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records.,contradicted,Consumers may assume compliance/audit history exists when only response-local event payloads are produced.\n5:This service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command,README.md:3,pyproject.toml exposes minisvc.cli:main as the `minisvc` console script; minisvc.api.routes:register_routes registers POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id>.,confirmed,Low; high-level product description matches the implementation.\n6:The fixture contains an HTTP adapter implementation that can run standalone,README.md:3 (implied by wording),minisvc.api.routes:register_routes expects an external app object and no server/bootstrap module exists in the repository.,unsupported,New engineers may spend time looking for a missing HTTP runtime or server entry point.\n7:"}],"details":{"totalLines":7,"displayContent":{"text":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\r\nMINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths,README.md:6,minisvc.config:load_settings parses readonly; minisvc.cli:main ignores Settings.readonly after load; minisvc.api.handlers:create_order always calls OrderRepository.save without a readonly check.,contradicted,Operators may believe writes are disabled when order creation still persists rows.\r\ncreate_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response,README.md:7,minisvc.api.handlers:create_order calls repo.save(order) exactly once; minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save performs one sqlite3 insert and has no retry loop or exception handling.,contradicted,Transient database failures surface directly and the service may be less resilient than documented.\r\nAudit events are stored in a durable audit table,README.md:8,minisvc.audit:order_event only returns a dict; minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records.,contradicted,Consumers may assume compliance/audit history exists when only response-local event payloads are produced.\r\nThis service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command,README.md:3,pyproject.toml exposes minisvc.cli:main as the `minisvc` console script; minisvc.api.routes:register_routes registers POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id>.,confirmed,Low; high-level product description matches the implementation.\r\nThe fixture contains an HTTP adapter implementation that can run standalone,README.md:3 (implied by wording),minisvc.api.routes:register_routes expects an external app object and no server/bootstrap module exists in the repository.,unsupported,New engineers may spend time looking for a missing HTTP runtime or server entry point.\r\n","startLine":1,"lineNumbers":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]},"fileSize":1793,"meta":{"source":{"type":"path","value":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"}}}},"isError":false}
